nt it to deviate from \"always gets its preferred size\""],["d40c9914_39450e7e",21,-1,0,"Is there any reason for this change?"],["f1ff863b_1655bfaa",21,-1,0,"Is this interior padding for the button? Would it make more sense to simply apply different margins?"],["22e5703e_77f67e48",21,0,1,"I am bit skeptical for allowing subclass to have access to `AddChildView` and `ReorderChildView` directly. Should we solve that from this change? It's ok for the other changes to be in a follow up CL."]],0,93],[7127263,20402,44,1.326,1.047,[[1,73]],[],0,94],[7139078,20403,154,4.195,3.394,[[1,1.0,74,156]],[["04a07ced_e1b67480",56,-1,1,"optional: Consider using kElementIdentifier instead of view Identifiers This is mainly preference, it should be fine either way since it is only used in this file 👍"],["5c438d93_226eb8d8",60,-1,1,"Add a function comment explaining what this function does / why we have it 👍"],["7330fa7e_0e7c2404",56,-1,1,"Instead of this would it help to add all of the right side views into a container view with it's own layout manager that way we don't have to manually calculate this? The implementation of this…"],["d313001a_59bc9d8f",56,0,1,"I believe this is only initialized when the kInfobarRefresh flag is enabled. There is potentially a crash here when `right_side_container_` is used. Let's do something like this: ``` if…"]],0,95],[7143218,20403,3,0.127,0.08,[[16,0]],[],0,96],[7148578,20404,15,0.439,0.29,[[8,0.429,5,7],[1,0.381,75,6],[9,0.095,3,1],[10,0.095,2,1]],[],0,97],[7147806,20405,89,2.344,1.853,[[1,76]],[["ea420364_1634af35",11,0,1,"Add a bug if there is one for this"]],0,98],[7152978,20405,26,0.721,0.543,[[1,77]],[],0,99],[7143178,20409,28,0.198,0.14,[[2,0.594,5,18],[1,0.406,78,10]],[["c97cdf7f_5face3b2",21,0,1,"Should we document what are we achieving here? It's not clear the relationship between a closeable infobar and a link. Ideally, the subclasses should not care about the child view added by the parent…"]],0,100],[7171724,20411,20,0.721,0.543,[[1,79]],[["d3235c47_d96e2f33",60,0,1,"I think we can undo this change since RecalculateLayoutBalancing() is only used within this class. Let's keep all of this stuff private for now 👍"]],0,101],[7169990,20411,18,0.198,0.14,[[2,6]],[],0,102],[7170801,20412,133,4.195,3.394,[[1,80]],[["00c39706_2fc02030",33,0,1,"nit: extra space"],["225f23d9_1e990ee7",33,0,1,"Since we have a global singleton class that manages instances of this object (`SessionRestoreInfoBarManager`), we should store this state inside that class instead of using global variables IMO."],["aad83056_3dbb6eec",33,0,0,"Does this guard is only for the shown / ignored metrics? what about the action_taken_for_session metric?"]],0,103],[7203104,20417,38,1.326,1.047,[[1,81]],[["61f2b4f4_a40289d4",61,0,1,"Does this is used?"]],0,104],[7213381,20423,4,0.248,0.178,[[1,82]],[],0,105],[7226895,20426,9,0.407,0.29,[[1,83]],[["00600259_9a90c873",62,0,1,"nit: remove"],["0062ab00_66b025f2",62,0,1,"Are these includes needed? All you are doing is referencing a feature below."],["a757ec3c_3533fe06",44,0,1,"This should moved up to keep it in alphabetical order as mentioned on the line 20-21"],["cd2eaf9f_0c039af1",10,0,1,"Should we at least document in the CL why it's enabled by default. Also it should be moved up."]],0,106],[7262634,20437,45,1.326,1.047,[[1,84]],[],0,107]]}